[{"id":3353720956,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7H5bh8","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"When preparing https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111557, I initially wanted to go for a SConstruct based approach as well.\r\nHowever, I got caught up on 2 problems:\r\n\r\n- I don't know an easy way to query the build system whether `libc++` is in use.\r\n- Editing `SConstruct` also affects thirdparty libraries, some of which break.\r\n\r\nIt seems like you've run into both as well, and decided to tackle them instead.\r\nYour approach should work everywhere, but ends up a bit more complicated than https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111557, and has to make some 'educated guesses' about when libc++ is used.\r\n\r\nMy approach (changing `typedefs.h`) is stupid simple. But it doesn't help in all compile units (depending on include order), and comes with a small risk of unexpected missing includes in headers, depending on include order of the compile unit.\r\n\r\nI'd be fine with choosing either. Maybe time for more people to weigh in?","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#pullrequestreview-3353720956","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111767","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#pullrequestreview-3353720956"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111767"}},"submitted_at":"2025-10-18T18:46:32Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3354310858,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7H7rjK","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Overall, after thinking about it some more, I think i prefer your approach.\nBut maybe we can simplify it some more?\n\nInstead of patching 3rd party libraries, can we just selectively disable `_LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES` on those that don't support it? That seems easier to maintain.\n\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111767#pullrequestreview-3354310858","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godo